WEBVTT

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:50.032
The Oxford Bookworms Library Stage 1 Sherlock Holmes and the Duke's Son by Sir Arthur Conan Doyle Text Adaptation by Jennifer Bassett Read by Richard Mitchley Copyright Oxford University Press 2002 Chapter 1 Sherlock Holmes has a Visitor When visitors came to see Sherlock Holmes in Baker Street, they often did surprising things.

00:00:50.092 --> 00:00:55.607
Sometimes they put their heads in their hands and cried.

00:00:55.666 --> 00:01:00.771
Sometimes they talked and talked and couldn't stop.

00:01:00.831 --> 00:01:07.204
and sometimes they just sat there and didn't say a word.

00:01:07.264 --> 00:01:14.218
But nobody was more surprising than Dr. Thornycroft Huxtable.

00:01:14.278 --> 00:01:22.192
He was a large man, tall, well dressed and important looking.

00:01:22.252 --> 00:01:31.514
He came into the room, walked to one of the big chairs and suddenly fell into it.

00:01:31.574 --> 00:01:38.446
He sat there with his eyes closed, looking white and ill.

00:01:38.506 --> 00:01:42.148
I ran to get some water for him.

00:01:42.208 --> 00:01:48.140
Then I got my doctor's bag and looked at him carefully.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.322
What is it, Watson?

00:01:50.382 --> 00:01:52.133
Said Holmes.

00:01:52.192 --> 00:01:56.595
He's all right, I think, I said.

00:01:56.655 --> 00:02:00.426
He's just very, very tired.

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:03.986
and probably hungry too.

00:02:04.046 --> 00:02:13.712
Holmes looked in the man's pockets and found a train ticket from Mackelton in the north of England.

00:02:13.771 --> 00:02:19.664
Mackelton, that's a long way, said Holmes.

00:02:19.724 --> 00:02:29.284
It's not twelve o'clock yet, so he probably left home before five o'clock this morning.

00:02:29.344 --> 00:02:37.172
After a minute or two, the man began to move, and his eyes opened.

00:02:37.231 --> 00:02:41.804
A second later, he got quickly to his feet.

00:02:41.864 --> 00:02:46.256
His face was now red and unhappy.

00:02:46.316 --> 00:02:50.147
Mr. Holmes, I am so sorry.

00:02:50.207 --> 00:02:54.329
I forgot to eat or drink anything this morning.

00:02:54.389 --> 00:02:57.180
That's why I felt ill.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.449
When you feel better I began.

00:03:01.508 --> 00:03:06.462
I'm better now, thank you," said our visitor.

00:03:06.522 --> 00:03:14.058
And I want very much to talk to Mr. Holmes, to ask him something.

00:03:14.118 --> 00:03:21.464
Please, Mr. Holmes, come back to Mackelton with me by the next train.

00:03:21.523 --> 00:03:26.678
I'm sorry, that's not possible, said Holmes.

00:03:26.738 --> 00:03:34.860
I'm working on two important cases the Ferris case and the Abagavenny case.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:38.782
I cannot leave London at the moment.

00:03:38.842 --> 00:03:48.070
Important cases are visitor-cried, but this case is very important too.

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:55.757
You know about the kidnapping of the son of the Duke of Holderness three days ago.

00:03:55.816 --> 00:03:57.088
What?

00:03:57.148 --> 00:03:59.346
The government minister?

00:03:59.406 --> 00:04:01.704
Yes, that's him.

00:04:01.764 --> 00:04:04.535
So, you didn't know.

00:04:04.595 --> 00:04:08.897
It's not in the newspapers yet, that's true.

00:04:08.957 --> 00:04:15.650
But Sherlock Holmes always hears news before other people, I thought.

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:25.438
Holmes went to get one of his books and began to read the page about the Duke of Holderness.

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:46.136
Holdiness, Sixth Duke, Wife, Edith, Daughter of Lord Gray, One Child, Lord Arthur Saltire, Houses in London, Lancashire, and Wales.

00:04:46.196 --> 00:04:53.200
Government Minister for this, for that, for the other.

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:56.690
Well, well, said Holmes.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:01.010
He is one of the greatest men in the country.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:08.836
One of the greatest and one of the richest, said Dr. Huxtable.

00:05:08.896 --> 00:05:14.120
I know, Mr. Holmes, that you don't work for money.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:17.212
But I must tell you this.

00:05:17.272 --> 00:05:24.722
The Duke is offering five thousand pounds for news of his son.

00:05:24.782 --> 00:05:31.812
and another 1,000 pounds for the name of his kidnapper.

00:05:31.872 --> 00:05:37.937
That, said Holmes, is a most interesting offer.

00:05:37.997 --> 00:05:40.068
He looked at me.

00:05:40.128 --> 00:05:41.690
What's it?

00:05:41.749 --> 00:05:49.616
I think we are going with Dr. Huxtable back to the north of England this afternoon.

00:05:49.676 --> 00:05:53.957
Holmes then looked at Dr. Huxtable.

00:05:54.017 --> 00:05:58.246
Now, sir, tell me everything.

00:05:58.306 --> 00:06:00.077
What happened?

00:06:00.137 --> 00:06:02.358
When did it happen?

00:06:02.418 --> 00:06:04.839
How did it happen?

00:06:04.899 --> 00:06:14.102
And why does Dr. Thornecraft Huxtable come to ask for my help three days later?

00:06:14.162 --> 00:06:21.962
Our visitor drank some water and began his story.

00:06:22.022 --> 00:06:25.778
CHAPTER II.

00:06:25.838 --> 00:06:33.893
DR. HUXEDIBLE STORY.

00:06:33.953 --> 00:06:48.451
My school, the Priory School, near Mackelton, is the best school for young boys in England.

00:06:48.511 --> 00:06:51.080
began Dr. Huxedible.

00:06:51.140 --> 00:07:00.020
We have the sons of Lord Son's, Lord Lever, and of many other important people.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:09.602
Three weeks ago, Mr. James Wilder, the Duke of Holderness' secretary, came to see me.

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:18.940
The Duke, he said, wanted to send his son, the ten-year-old Lord Sultyre, to my school.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:24.678
On the first of May, young Lord Sultyre arrived.

00:07:24.738 --> 00:07:32.541
He's a nice boy, and he soon began to like school life, and to make friends.

00:07:32.601 --> 00:07:38.194
His life at home, you see, was not very happy.

00:07:38.254 --> 00:07:42.596
We all know about the Duke and his wife.

00:07:42.656 --> 00:07:53.442
The Duchess, of course, now lives in the south of France, She left the Duke about three months ago, I think.

00:07:53.502 --> 00:08:00.664
But the boy loved his mother and was very unhappy when she left.

00:08:00.724 --> 00:08:06.114
Because of this, the Duke sent him to my school.

00:08:06.174 --> 00:08:11.976
And after two weeks with us, he was much happier.

00:08:12.036 --> 00:08:19.076
Then, on the night of the 13th of May, he disappeared.

00:08:19.136 --> 00:08:24.918
The way to his bedroom is through another larger room.

00:08:24.978 --> 00:08:28.430
Two older boys sleep there.

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:36.415
One of them never sleeps very well, and he heard and saw nothing that night.

00:08:36.476 --> 00:08:41.888
So young Arthur did not go out through that room.

00:08:41.948 --> 00:08:49.288
His window was open, and there is ivy all up the wall of the house.

00:08:49.348 --> 00:08:55.833
It is easy to get out of the window and down the ivy to the ground.

00:08:55.893 --> 00:09:00.474
So we think that he went out that way.

00:09:00.534 --> 00:09:10.316
He was in his usual school things, we think, a short black coat and dark blue trousers.

00:09:10.376 --> 00:09:20.450
We looked all through his room very carefully, but we found nothing strange, nothing unusual.

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:31.705
When I learnt the news at seven o'clock on Tuesday morning, I called everybody into the big school room.

00:09:31.725 --> 00:09:34.616
Then we learnt more bad news.

00:09:34.676 --> 00:09:39.828
Heidegger, the German teacher, was missing too.

00:09:39.888 --> 00:09:44.791
His room is not far from Arthur's room.

00:09:44.851 --> 00:09:48.222
Heidegger went down the ivy.

00:09:48.282 --> 00:09:49.668
We know this.

00:09:49.728 --> 00:09:55.356
because we found his footprints on the ground under the window.

00:09:55.416 --> 00:10:08.832
We know too that he was only in his coat, trousers and shoes, because we found his shirt and his socks on the floor of his room.

00:10:08.892 --> 00:10:13.184
And he took his bicycle with him.

00:10:13.244 --> 00:10:17.446
Heidegger came to the school a year ago.

00:10:17.506 --> 00:10:25.280
He's a good teacher but the boys don't like him because he isn't very friendly.

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:30.614
So, Mr. Holmes, we have two missing people.

00:10:30.674 --> 00:10:36.329
It's now Thursday and there's still no news of them.

00:10:36.389 --> 00:10:42.504
Holmes took out a little notebook and began to write things down.

00:10:42.564 --> 00:10:47.298
The boy didn't go home, of course, he said.

00:10:47.358 --> 00:10:48.516
No, no.

00:10:48.576 --> 00:10:53.568
We asked at Holden this hall at once, said Dr. Huxtable.

00:10:53.627 --> 00:11:01.164
The Duke is very afraid for his son, and I am the unhappiest man in England.

00:11:01.224 --> 00:11:05.018
Mr. Holmes, you are a famous detective.

00:11:05.078 --> 00:11:07.290
Please help me.

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:12.536
You make things very difficult for me, Holmes said.

00:11:12.596 --> 00:11:19.800
How can I find marks in the ivy or on the ground after three days?

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:23.492
Why didn't you come to me at once?

00:11:23.551 --> 00:11:28.324
Because of the duke, Dr. Huxtable said.

00:11:28.384 --> 00:11:34.416
He doesn't like people talking about his unhappy family life.

00:11:34.476 --> 00:11:37.718
And what are the police doing?

00:11:37.778 --> 00:11:46.260
Well, they heard about a boy and a young man at the station early on Tuesday.

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:58.402
They looked for them, and last night they found them in Liverpool, but it was a man and his son going to visit a friend.

00:11:58.462 --> 00:12:06.282
We lost three days because of that, and last night I couldn't sleep.

00:12:06.342 --> 00:12:11.342
So I took the first train down to London this morning.

00:12:11.402 --> 00:12:17.574
Well, Dr. Huxtable, some more questions, said Holmes.

00:12:17.634 --> 00:12:21.266
Did the boy take German lessons?

00:12:21.326 --> 00:12:22.656
No.

00:12:22.716 --> 00:12:27.548
So he didn't know the German teacher well then.

00:12:27.608 --> 00:12:32.701
He probably never spoke to him, said Dr. Huxtable.

00:12:32.761 --> 00:12:35.598
Hmm, said Holmes.

00:12:35.658 --> 00:12:38.766
Does the boy have a bicycle?

00:12:38.826 --> 00:12:40.236
No.

00:12:40.296 --> 00:12:43.677
Was any other bicycle missing?

00:12:43.737 --> 00:12:45.188
No.

00:12:45.248 --> 00:12:54.600
So, did the German teacher ride away on his bicycle in the night with the boy on his back?

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:57.011
I don't think so.

00:12:57.071 --> 00:13:00.472
But what happened to the bicycle?

00:13:00.532 --> 00:13:04.300
Now, what about visitors?

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:08.389
Did the boy have any visitors the day before?

00:13:08.449 --> 00:13:10.009
No.

00:13:10.069 --> 00:13:12.840
Did he get any letters?

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:17.450
Yes, one letter from his father.

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:21.752
Do you open the boy's letters, Dr. Huxtable?

00:13:21.812 --> 00:13:23.242
No.

00:13:23.302 --> 00:13:28.123
Then how do you know that the letter was from the father?

00:13:28.183 --> 00:13:35.216
I know the Duke's handwriting, and he says that he wrote a letter to his son.

00:13:35.276 --> 00:13:39.800
Did the boy get any letters from France?

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:43.452
No, I never saw any.

00:13:43.512 --> 00:13:47.344
Do you understand me, Dr. Huxtable?

00:13:47.404 --> 00:13:48.704
Holmes said.

00:13:48.764 --> 00:13:52.346
Did someone take the boy away?

00:13:52.406 --> 00:13:55.928
Or did the boy go freely?

00:13:55.988 --> 00:14:00.541
Because he had a letter from France, perhaps.

00:14:00.601 --> 00:14:04.667
I don't know, said Dr. Huxtable.

00:14:04.727 --> 00:14:09.434
He only had letters from his father, I think.

00:14:09.494 --> 00:14:14.038
We're father and son very friendly.

00:14:14.098 --> 00:14:21.103
The Duke is not a very friendly man, Mr. Holmes.

00:14:21.163 --> 00:14:30.060
He's not a bad father, but he is a government minister and has a lot of things to do.

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:35.035
So the boy felt more friendly to his mother.

00:14:35.095 --> 00:14:36.387
Yes.

00:14:36.448 --> 00:14:38.398
Did he say that?

00:14:38.458 --> 00:14:39.670
No.

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:42.701
Did the Duke tell you them?

00:14:42.761 --> 00:14:43.972
Oh, no.

00:14:44.032 --> 00:14:47.914
The Duke never talks about things like that.

00:14:47.974 --> 00:14:50.085
So how do you know?

00:14:50.105 --> 00:14:56.188
Mr. James Wilder, the Duke's secretary, told me.

00:14:56.248 --> 00:14:59.620
I see, said Holmes.

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:04.552
That last letter of the dukes, where is it now?

00:15:04.612 --> 00:15:09.044
The boy took it with him, Dr. Huxtable said.

00:15:09.104 --> 00:15:11.507
It's not in his room.

00:15:11.567 --> 00:15:16.592
Mr. Holmes, our train leaves in half an hour.

00:15:16.652 --> 00:15:19.024
Right, said Holmes.

00:15:19.084 --> 00:15:20.636
He looked at me.

00:15:20.696 --> 00:15:26.921
Watson, let's get ready and go off to the north with Dr. Huxtable.

00:15:26.981 --> 00:15:33.820
Perhaps we can find some answers to this mystery.

00:15:33.880 --> 00:15:46.018
Chapter 3, Holmes and Watson Go North.

00:15:46.078 --> 00:16:00.224
It was dark when we arrived at Dr. Huxtable's famous school in the Northern Hills.

00:16:00.284 --> 00:16:05.616
We went quickly into the building out of the cold.

00:16:05.676 --> 00:16:12.684
And at once, someone ran up with news that Dr. Huxtable.

00:16:12.743 --> 00:16:16.486
He looked very surprised.

00:16:16.546 --> 00:16:20.671
The Duke is here, he told us.

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:30.338
The Duke and Mr. Wilder, his secretary, are in my office and come and meet them.

00:16:30.398 --> 00:16:35.137
The government minister was a tall man.

00:16:35.197 --> 00:16:38.424
with a long, thin face.

00:16:38.484 --> 00:16:44.007
He had red hair and a great red beard.

00:16:44.068 --> 00:16:48.680
He looked at us and did not smile.

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:55.034
Next to him stood Mr. Wilder, a very young man.

00:16:55.094 --> 00:17:00.828
He was small with blue eyes and a watchful face.

00:17:00.887 --> 00:17:10.845
He spoke first The Duke is surprised, Dr. Huxtable, to see Mr. Sherlock Holmes here.

00:17:10.906 --> 00:17:15.308
He doesn't want people to know about this.

00:17:15.368 --> 00:17:17.479
You know that.

00:17:17.539 --> 00:17:23.873
So why didn't you speak to the Duke before you went to London?

00:17:23.934 --> 00:17:28.686
But we need help, said Dr. Huxtable.

00:17:28.746 --> 00:17:29.846
And I...

00:17:29.906 --> 00:17:32.903
Well, said the Duke.

00:17:32.963 --> 00:17:39.810
Mr. Holmes is here now, and perhaps he can help us.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:42.962
He looked at Holmes.

00:17:43.022 --> 00:17:49.774
I'd like you to come and stay at Holderness Hall, Mr. Holmes.

00:17:49.834 --> 00:17:53.966
Thank you, sir, said Holmes.

00:17:54.026 --> 00:18:00.946
But I would like to stay near to the mystery, here at the school.

00:18:01.007 --> 00:18:05.878
Can I ask you one or two questions, perhaps?

00:18:05.938 --> 00:18:09.370
Of course, said the Duke.

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:17.556
My questions are about the Duchess and about money, said Holmes.

00:18:17.616 --> 00:18:27.253
The Duchess knows nothing about this, said the Duke, and nobody is asking me for money.

00:18:27.313 --> 00:18:30.779
I see, said Holmes.

00:18:30.839 --> 00:18:36.555
You wrote a letter to your son before he disappeared.

00:18:36.615 --> 00:18:39.436
When did you post it?

00:18:39.496 --> 00:18:43.927
Post it, said Mr. Wilder angrily.

00:18:43.987 --> 00:18:47.228
The duke does not post letters.

00:18:47.288 --> 00:18:54.692
I put the letter into the post bag with all the other letters that day.

00:18:54.752 --> 00:19:00.994
A minute or two later, the duke and Mr. Wilder left.

00:19:01.054 --> 00:19:06.568
Holmes then began at once to work on the case.

00:19:06.628 --> 00:19:14.230
We looked carefully all through the boy's bedroom and the German teacher's room.

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:23.814
We looked at the ivy on the wall, and we saw the footprints under the German teacher's window.

00:19:23.875 --> 00:19:27.716
But we learnt nothing new.

00:19:27.776 --> 00:19:35.873
Holmes then left the house and only came back after 11 o'clock.

00:19:35.933 --> 00:19:40.517
He had with him a large map.

00:19:40.577 --> 00:19:46.251
He brought it into my room and put it on the bed.

00:19:46.312 --> 00:19:52.816
This case is beginning to get interesting, Watson, he said.

00:19:52.876 --> 00:19:55.418
Look at this map.

00:19:55.478 --> 00:20:01.217
Here is the school, you see, and here is the road.

00:20:01.277 --> 00:20:08.554
So, did the boy and the teacher go along the road when they left?

00:20:08.615 --> 00:20:11.936
No, Watson, they did not.

00:20:11.996 --> 00:20:15.307
How do you know that, Holmes?

00:20:15.367 --> 00:20:16.867
I asked.

00:20:16.928 --> 00:20:30.048
Because there was a policeman here, look, he was there from midnight to six in the morning, and he saw nobody on the road.

00:20:30.108 --> 00:20:33.415
I spoke to him this evening.

00:20:33.475 --> 00:20:40.440
And here, at the other end, you see, is the white horse in.

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:50.048
A woman there was ill, and the family watched the road all night, waiting for the doctor.

00:20:50.108 --> 00:20:58.837
The doctor didn't come until the morning, and the family saw nobody on the road.

00:20:58.897 --> 00:21:04.992
The boy and the teacher did not go by road.

00:21:05.052 --> 00:21:08.964
But Holmes, what about the bicycle?

00:21:09.024 --> 00:21:10.494
I asked.

00:21:10.554 --> 00:21:12.635
Yes, Watson.

00:21:12.695 --> 00:21:16.416
We must remember the bicycle, of course.

00:21:16.476 --> 00:21:22.078
But first, let's look to the south and the north.

00:21:22.138 --> 00:21:26.049
To the south, we have a big river.

00:21:26.109 --> 00:21:29.128
No bicycles there then.

00:21:29.188 --> 00:21:41.480
and to the north we have the trees called ragged shore, and then a great moor, the lower gill moor.

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:55.226
And here is holdonous hall, sixteen kilometres from the school by road, but only nine kilometres across the moor.

00:21:55.286 --> 00:22:03.234
No other houses until the green man in along the Chesterfield Road.

00:22:03.294 --> 00:22:07.107
But the bicycle, I said again.

00:22:07.168 --> 00:22:11.182
Yes, yes, Watson, Holmes said.

00:22:11.242 --> 00:22:18.898
It is possible to ride a bicycle across the moor, difficult but possible.

00:22:18.958 --> 00:22:24.772
Just then, Dr. Huxtable came quickly into the room.

00:22:24.832 --> 00:22:26.892
News, Mr. Holmes!

00:22:26.952 --> 00:22:30.962
He said excitedly, I bring news.

00:22:31.022 --> 00:22:35.796
In his hands was a blue school hat.

00:22:35.856 --> 00:22:39.498
Look, this is the boy's hat.

00:22:39.558 --> 00:22:43.710
One of my gardeners found it this evening.

00:22:43.770 --> 00:22:45.242
Where, man?

00:22:45.302 --> 00:22:46.222
Where?

00:22:46.282 --> 00:22:47.874
asked Holmes.

00:22:47.934 --> 00:22:51.296
Just north of ragged shore.

00:22:51.356 --> 00:22:53.358
Said Dr. Huxdable.

00:22:53.418 --> 00:22:54.858
Aha!

00:22:54.918 --> 00:22:56.309
Said Holmes.

00:22:56.370 --> 00:22:59.341
What did I tell you, Watson?

00:22:59.401 --> 00:23:05.702
Tomorrow we must walk north across the moor.

00:23:05.762 --> 00:23:30.128
Chapter 4 The Body on the More Very early the next morning I opened my eyes and saw homes next to my bed.

00:23:30.188 --> 00:23:32.400
He was already dressed.

00:23:32.420 --> 00:23:35.802
"'Come, Watson,' he cried.

00:23:35.822 --> 00:23:38.954
"'There is hot coffee ready for you.

00:23:39.014 --> 00:23:42.317
We leave in ten minutes.'

00:23:42.377 --> 00:23:52.874
By six o'clock we were through ragged shore, and half an hour later we were on lower gill moor.

00:23:52.934 --> 00:24:03.302
Across the middle of the moor was a small river, and the ground all around it was very wet.

00:24:03.363 --> 00:24:10.124
We can easily see tracks in this wet ground, said Holmes.

00:24:10.184 --> 00:24:13.236
Look carefully, Watson.

00:24:13.296 --> 00:24:20.867
We moved slowly across the moor, looking at every centimeter of mud.

00:24:20.927 --> 00:24:31.096
We found hundreds of sheep tracks and once some cow tracks, but no bicycle tracks.

00:24:31.156 --> 00:24:35.988
And then, at last, we found something.

00:24:36.048 --> 00:24:46.364
Not far from the little river, right across some nice black mud was the track of a bicycle.

00:24:46.424 --> 00:24:48.004
Hoorah!

00:24:48.064 --> 00:24:48.955
I cried.

00:24:49.015 --> 00:24:50.415
We have it!

00:24:50.476 --> 00:24:54.288
But Holmes did not look happy.

00:24:54.348 --> 00:25:00.354
It's a bicycle, yes, but not the bicycle.

00:25:00.414 --> 00:25:04.356
Every bicycle has different tires.

00:25:04.416 --> 00:25:09.150
I know forty-two different kinds of tire.

00:25:09.210 --> 00:25:16.646
This tire is a Dunlop, but Heidegger's bicycle had Palmer tires.

00:25:16.706 --> 00:25:19.838
The English teacher told me that.

00:25:19.898 --> 00:25:23.116
So this is not Heidegger.

00:25:23.176 --> 00:25:25.413
Is it the boy then?"

00:25:25.473 --> 00:25:26.784
I asked.

00:25:26.844 --> 00:25:28.864
Probably not.

00:25:28.924 --> 00:25:34.485
The boy didn't take a bicycle with him, said Holmes.

00:25:34.545 --> 00:25:38.426
He looked again at the track in the mud.

00:25:38.486 --> 00:25:42.947
This track is going away from the school.

00:25:43.007 --> 00:25:46.878
Or perhaps to the school, I said.

00:25:46.938 --> 00:25:49.388
No, no, my dear Watson.

00:25:49.448 --> 00:25:52.800
Look at the tracks of the two tires.

00:25:52.860 --> 00:25:55.271
Are they the same?

00:25:55.332 --> 00:25:58.223
No, I said.

00:25:58.283 --> 00:26:02.036
One tire makes a deeper track.

00:26:02.096 --> 00:26:11.640
And that's the back wheel, said Holmes, because the rider, of course, sits over the back wheel.

00:26:11.701 --> 00:26:15.943
The deeper track is the one on top.

00:26:16.003 --> 00:26:23.421
So this bicycle went that way, across the moor, away from the school.

00:26:23.481 --> 00:26:26.306
But who was the rider?

00:26:26.366 --> 00:26:29.116
Where did he come from?

00:26:29.176 --> 00:26:34.927
We followed the Dunlop track back, nearly to ragged shore.

00:26:34.987 --> 00:26:39.358
Then we lost it in some cow tracks.

00:26:39.418 --> 00:26:44.539
Holmes sat down and thought for some minutes.

00:26:44.599 --> 00:26:48.240
Nope, he said, getting up.

00:26:48.300 --> 00:26:51.414
We must leave this question for now.

00:26:51.474 --> 00:26:55.428
Back to the mud by the river Watson.

00:26:55.488 --> 00:27:00.711
Two hours later, Holmes gave a happy cry.

00:27:00.771 --> 00:27:08.905
I quickly ran over to him and looked down at a long, thin track in the mud.

00:27:08.965 --> 00:27:12.156
It was the Palmer tyre.

00:27:12.216 --> 00:27:16.088
Here is Heidegger, cried Holmes.

00:27:16.148 --> 00:27:19.212
Let's follow him Watson.

00:27:19.272 --> 00:27:32.912
For a kilometer or more, we followed the parmatire north across the moor, losing the track, finding it again, losing it, and finding it.

00:27:32.972 --> 00:27:36.714
Suddenly the track stopped.

00:27:36.774 --> 00:27:38.986
What happened here?

00:27:39.046 --> 00:27:42.498
I said, did he fall?

00:27:42.558 --> 00:27:46.548
Holmes looked carefully on the ground.

00:27:46.608 --> 00:27:52.496
Then he moved to some small bushes with yellow flowers on them.

00:27:52.557 --> 00:27:56.338
Look, he said quietly.

00:27:56.398 --> 00:28:06.414
On one of the yellow flowers, there was something red, the dark brownie red of blood.

00:28:06.474 --> 00:28:09.866
Bad, said Holmes.

00:28:09.926 --> 00:28:11.397
Bad.

00:28:11.457 --> 00:28:13.828
What do I read here?

00:28:13.888 --> 00:28:17.326
Something or someone hit him.

00:28:17.386 --> 00:28:18.822
He fell.

00:28:18.882 --> 00:28:20.304
He stood up.

00:28:20.364 --> 00:28:25.348
He got onto his bicycle again and rode away.

00:28:25.408 --> 00:28:28.830
But there is no other track.

00:28:28.890 --> 00:28:33.844
Some cow tracks here, but no footprints.

00:28:33.904 --> 00:28:37.947
We must follow the blood, Watson.

00:28:38.007 --> 00:28:41.490
We soon found the bicycle.

00:28:41.550 --> 00:28:48.218
And then, behind a bush, we saw a shoe and found a body.

00:28:48.279 --> 00:28:56.216
There was blood on the man's head and face, and he was very, very dead.

00:28:56.277 --> 00:29:00.168
He had shoes on, but no socks.

00:29:00.228 --> 00:29:04.550
And we saw a night shirt under his open coat.

00:29:04.610 --> 00:29:08.102
It was the German teacher.

00:29:08.162 --> 00:29:12.484
Poor man, home said quietly.

00:29:12.544 --> 00:29:15.134
What shall we do, Watson?

00:29:15.194 --> 00:29:18.522
We can't lose any more time.

00:29:18.582 --> 00:29:23.078
But we must tell someone about this poor man.

00:29:23.138 --> 00:29:26.799
Shall I run back to the school?"

00:29:26.859 --> 00:29:28.269
I said.

00:29:28.330 --> 00:29:32.701
No, I need you with me.

00:29:32.761 --> 00:29:37.252
Holmes stood up and looked around.

00:29:37.312 --> 00:29:40.253
Look, he said.

00:29:40.313 --> 00:29:43.364
There's a workman over there.

00:29:43.424 --> 00:29:48.171
He can go back to the school for us.

00:29:48.231 --> 00:29:56.762
I went and got the workman, and Holmes wrote a note for Dr. Huxtable.

00:29:56.822 --> 00:30:07.820
The poor workman took one look at the body and began to run quickly down the hill to ragged shore.

00:30:07.880 --> 00:30:17.728
Now, said Holmes, before we go on, let's think carefully for a minute.

00:30:17.788 --> 00:30:21.840
What do we know so far?

00:30:21.900 --> 00:30:26.180
First, the boy left freely.

00:30:26.240 --> 00:30:28.261
He was dressed.

00:30:28.321 --> 00:30:31.282
He did not leave suddenly.

00:30:31.342 --> 00:30:33.632
He wanted to go.

00:30:33.692 --> 00:30:36.183
Perhaps with someone?

00:30:36.243 --> 00:30:38.324
Perhaps not.

00:30:38.384 --> 00:30:45.996
But the German teacher left without his socks and without his shirt.

00:30:46.057 --> 00:30:49.790
So he left very suddenly.

00:30:49.850 --> 00:30:53.332
That's right, I said.

00:30:53.392 --> 00:30:57.064
And why did Heidegger go?

00:30:57.124 --> 00:31:03.607
Because from his bedroom window, he saw the boy.

00:31:03.668 --> 00:31:09.000
Because he wanted to follow him and bring him back.

00:31:09.060 --> 00:31:12.176
So far, so good.

00:31:12.236 --> 00:31:18.532
But why doesn't Heidegger just run after the boy?

00:31:18.592 --> 00:31:23.494
A man can easily run faster than a boy.

00:31:23.554 --> 00:31:27.106
But Heidegger doesn't do this.

00:31:27.166 --> 00:31:30.006
He gets his bicycle.

00:31:30.066 --> 00:31:34.138
He knows that he needs his bicycle.

00:31:34.198 --> 00:31:36.258
Why?

00:31:36.318 --> 00:31:42.414
Ah, I said, because the boy has a bicycle.

00:31:42.474 --> 00:31:45.559
Not so fast, Watson.

00:31:45.620 --> 00:31:48.052
Think about it.

00:31:48.112 --> 00:31:53.756
Heidegger dies eight kilometers from the school.

00:31:53.816 --> 00:32:06.008
So the boy is moving very fast, because it is eight kilometers before a man on a bicycle can get near him.

00:32:06.067 --> 00:32:14.345
And Heidegger dies because someone hits him very hard on the head.

00:32:14.405 --> 00:32:17.516
A boy can't do that.

00:32:17.576 --> 00:32:21.537
So there was someone with the boy.

00:32:21.597 --> 00:32:24.478
A man, let's say.

00:32:24.538 --> 00:32:32.631
But we looked very carefully at the mud all round poor Heidegger's body wasm.

00:32:32.691 --> 00:32:35.252
And what did we find?

00:32:35.312 --> 00:32:39.467
Some cow tracks, but nothing more.

00:32:39.527 --> 00:32:42.692
No footprints from people.

00:32:42.752 --> 00:32:45.432
No bicycle tracks.

00:32:45.492 --> 00:32:48.103
Holmes, I cried.

00:32:48.163 --> 00:32:50.663
This is not possible.

00:32:50.723 --> 00:32:54.514
Very good, Watson, he said.

00:32:54.574 --> 00:32:56.854
It's not possible.

00:32:56.914 --> 00:33:01.065
So something is wrong with my thinking.

00:33:01.125 --> 00:33:03.736
What can it be?

00:33:03.796 --> 00:33:10.271
Perhaps, I said, Heidegger broke his head in a fall.

00:33:10.331 --> 00:33:13.186
In mud, Watson?

00:33:13.246 --> 00:33:15.057
Oh, I don't know.

00:33:15.077 --> 00:33:17.198
I just don't know.

00:33:17.258 --> 00:33:21.300
Come, come, Watson," said Holmes.

00:33:21.360 --> 00:33:24.802
Every mystery has an answer.

00:33:24.862 --> 00:33:31.156
But for now, the Palmer tyre can tell us nothing more.

00:33:31.216 --> 00:33:36.479
So we must go back to the Dunlop tyre.

00:33:36.539 --> 00:33:40.473
We found the Dunlop track again.

00:33:40.533 --> 00:33:43.096
and followed it north.

00:33:43.156 --> 00:33:49.688
Here there was very little mud, and we lost the track.

00:33:49.748 --> 00:34:03.903
Across the moor we could now see Holderness Hall, some kilometres to our left, and in front of us we could see the Chesterfield Road.

00:34:03.963 --> 00:34:11.538
We walked down to the road and along to the Green Man Inn.

00:34:11.597 --> 00:34:23.228
Chapter 5 A Visit to the Green Man.

00:34:23.288 --> 00:34:34.478
When we were near the inn, Holmes suddenly cried out.

00:34:34.538 --> 00:34:35.428
Ah!

00:34:35.489 --> 00:34:36.679
My foot!

00:34:36.740 --> 00:34:38.782
I can't stand on it.

00:34:38.842 --> 00:34:41.063
Help me Watson.

00:34:41.123 --> 00:34:43.393
I took his arm.

00:34:43.454 --> 00:34:47.823
and we walked slowly to the door of the inn.

00:34:47.883 --> 00:34:53.514
A man stood there, smoking and watching us.

00:34:53.575 --> 00:34:57.395
How are you, Mr. Ruben Hayes?

00:34:57.455 --> 00:34:59.376
said Holmes.

00:34:59.436 --> 00:35:01.376
Who are you?

00:35:01.436 --> 00:35:04.357
And how do you know my name?

00:35:04.417 --> 00:35:06.078
Said the man.

00:35:06.138 --> 00:35:09.218
He looked very unfriendly.

00:35:09.278 --> 00:35:12.422
Because it's on the door of the inn.

00:35:12.482 --> 00:35:15.708
Over your head, said Holmes.

00:35:15.768 --> 00:35:19.272
But can you help me, Mr. Hayes?

00:35:19.332 --> 00:35:21.734
No, I can't.

00:35:21.794 --> 00:35:24.326
But I need help.

00:35:24.386 --> 00:35:28.108
I can't put my foot to the ground.

00:35:28.168 --> 00:35:31.932
Well, don't put it to the ground."

00:35:31.992 --> 00:35:34.453
Holmes smiled.

00:35:34.514 --> 00:35:36.806
Look, he said.

00:35:36.866 --> 00:35:39.344
It's very important.

00:35:39.404 --> 00:35:45.194
and I can offer you a pound for the use of a bicycle.

00:35:45.254 --> 00:35:48.255
Where do you want to go?"

00:35:48.316 --> 00:35:50.396
asked Mr. Hayes.

00:35:50.456 --> 00:35:53.198
To Holdeness Hall.

00:35:53.258 --> 00:35:54.549
Oh!

00:35:54.609 --> 00:35:57.370
Friends of the Duke, are you?

00:35:57.430 --> 00:36:03.333
Mr. Hayes laughed, looking at our muddy shoes and trousers.

00:36:03.394 --> 00:36:06.410
Holmes laughed, too.

00:36:06.470 --> 00:36:12.471
"'Well, we are bringing him news of his lost son,' he said.

00:36:12.491 --> 00:36:16.985
"'The boy is in Liverpool.'

00:36:17.045 --> 00:36:20.177
Mr. Hayes' face went white, then red.

00:36:20.197 --> 00:36:28.865
"'Oh,' he said carefully, "'that's good news.

00:36:28.925 --> 00:36:35.328
I worked for the Duke once, but he wasn't good to me.

00:36:35.388 --> 00:36:40.930
I don't like him, but I'm pleased about the boy."

00:36:40.991 --> 00:36:44.543
We all went into the inn.

00:36:44.603 --> 00:36:47.255
Now said Holmes.

00:36:47.315 --> 00:36:50.527
Something to eat first, please.

00:36:50.588 --> 00:36:54.310
Then you can bring round the bicycle.

00:36:54.370 --> 00:36:59.414
I haven't got a bicycle, said Mr. Hayes.

00:36:59.474 --> 00:37:03.846
Holmes put a pound on the table.

00:37:03.906 --> 00:37:08.897
I tell you, man, that I haven't got a bicycle.

00:37:08.957 --> 00:37:13.409
You can have two horses to take you to the hall."

00:37:13.470 --> 00:37:18.832
He brought us something to eat, and we ate hungrily.

00:37:18.893 --> 00:37:25.505
Through the window we could see the stables at the back of the inn.

00:37:25.566 --> 00:37:36.074
Once Holmes got up and walked round the room, Then stood, looking out of the window at the stables.

00:37:36.134 --> 00:37:41.947
Surprisingly, his foot was now very much better.

00:37:42.008 --> 00:37:46.330
Suddenly he laughed and looked at me.

00:37:46.390 --> 00:37:47.951
I've got it!

00:37:48.011 --> 00:37:49.382
He cried.

00:37:49.442 --> 00:37:51.833
Yes, of course!

00:37:51.893 --> 00:37:53.334
That's it!

00:37:53.394 --> 00:37:58.697
Watson, did you see any cow tracks today?

00:37:58.757 --> 00:38:01.070
Yes, I said.

00:38:01.130 --> 00:38:04.374
Lots of them, everywhere.

00:38:04.434 --> 00:38:09.638
And how many cows did you see on the moor?

00:38:09.698 --> 00:38:13.890
I don't remember any, I said.

00:38:13.950 --> 00:38:17.482
Isn't that strange, Watson?

00:38:17.542 --> 00:38:22.295
Lots of cow tracks, but no cows.

00:38:22.356 --> 00:38:27.148
And do you remember those tracks, Watson?

00:38:27.208 --> 00:38:30.242
He took out his notebook.

00:38:30.302 --> 00:38:37.788
There were tracks like this, and sometimes like this.

00:38:37.848 --> 00:38:41.640
And sometimes like this.

00:38:41.700 --> 00:38:45.010
Do you remember that, Watson?

00:38:45.070 --> 00:38:47.121
No, I don't.

00:38:47.182 --> 00:38:51.264
I said, what does it mean, Holmes?

00:38:51.324 --> 00:38:57.246
It means that it's a very strange cow, Watson.

00:38:57.306 --> 00:39:01.160
Cows don't move like that.

00:39:01.220 --> 00:39:09.980
Now, let's go quietly out and have a look round these stables.

00:39:10.040 --> 00:39:15.816
There were two tired looking horses in the stables.

00:39:15.877 --> 00:39:22.202
Homes looked carefully at one of the horses' feet and laughed.

00:39:22.263 --> 00:39:27.994
Look Watson, old shoes, but new nails!

00:39:28.054 --> 00:39:34.514
Oh, this case gets more interesting every minute.

00:39:34.574 --> 00:39:38.706
I began to ask Holmes a question.

00:39:38.766 --> 00:39:43.198
But suddenly we heard someone behind us.

00:39:43.258 --> 00:39:46.909
And there was Mr. Ruben Hayes.

00:39:46.969 --> 00:39:50.870
His face was red and angry.

00:39:50.930 --> 00:39:54.492
What are you doing in my stables?

00:39:54.552 --> 00:39:56.174
He cried.

00:39:56.234 --> 00:40:02.868
We're just looking at your horses, Mr. Hayes," said Holmes, smiling.

00:40:02.928 --> 00:40:04.278
Why?

00:40:04.339 --> 00:40:07.260
Are you afraid of something?

00:40:07.320 --> 00:40:12.612
The man opened his mouth, then closed it quickly.

00:40:12.672 --> 00:40:17.144
His face was still red and angry.

00:40:17.204 --> 00:40:21.776
Holmes did not give him time to speak.

00:40:21.836 --> 00:40:26.601
I think your horses are tired, Mr. Hayes.

00:40:26.661 --> 00:40:29.136
We can walk to the hall.

00:40:29.196 --> 00:40:31.407
It's not far.

00:40:31.467 --> 00:40:36.860
Three kilometers by the road, Mr. Hayes said.

00:40:36.920 --> 00:40:41.464
His eyes still watched us angrily.

00:40:41.524 --> 00:40:45.736
It was nearly dark when we left.

00:40:45.796 --> 00:40:50.560
We walked along the road for about a hundred meters.

00:40:50.620 --> 00:40:53.912
Then homes took my arm.

00:40:53.973 --> 00:40:55.766
Quick, Watson.

00:40:55.826 --> 00:40:58.972
off the road and up the hill.

00:40:59.032 --> 00:41:04.734
Then we can come down the hill at the back of the inn.

00:41:04.794 --> 00:41:08.046
We ran up the hill.

00:41:08.106 --> 00:41:11.688
This man haze, I said.

00:41:11.748 --> 00:41:14.870
He knows all about the kidnapping.

00:41:14.930 --> 00:41:17.070
Is that right, Holmes?

00:41:17.130 --> 00:41:20.492
Of course it is, he said.

00:41:20.553 --> 00:41:25.402
We can learn a lot more from Mr. Hayes.

00:41:25.462 --> 00:41:27.990
Who's this?

00:41:28.051 --> 00:41:30.863
Watson, get down.

00:41:30.923 --> 00:41:34.736
There was a bicycle on the road.

00:41:34.796 --> 00:41:40.442
It came past us very quickly, and we saw the rider.

00:41:40.502 --> 00:41:44.986
Mr. James Wilder, the Duke secretary.

00:41:45.046 --> 00:41:49.068
His face was white and afraid.

00:41:49.128 --> 00:41:52.391
Quick, Watson, said Holmes.

00:41:52.452 --> 00:41:54.755
We must watch him.

00:41:54.816 --> 00:42:02.540
we ran down the hill and stopped when we could see the back door of the inn.

00:42:02.600 --> 00:42:07.892
Wild as bicycle was by the wall near the door.

00:42:07.952 --> 00:42:11.794
For five minutes nothing happened.

00:42:11.854 --> 00:42:21.027
Then a man on a horse rode quickly out of the stables and disappeared down the road.

00:42:21.087 --> 00:42:24.422
What do you think of that, Watson?

00:42:24.482 --> 00:42:26.116
said Holmes.

00:42:26.176 --> 00:42:28.766
Somebody's running away!

00:42:28.826 --> 00:42:36.759
Yes, but not James Wilder, because there he is at the door.

00:42:36.820 --> 00:42:41.502
We could see Wilder in the light from the door.

00:42:41.562 --> 00:42:52.024
He stood there looking out, and ten minutes later another man came down the road and went into the inn.

00:42:52.084 --> 00:42:57.486
Then a light came on in a room upstairs.

00:42:57.546 --> 00:43:03.700
Come, Watson, we must get nearer, Holmes said.

00:43:03.760 --> 00:43:12.326
We went down the hill and walked very quietly to the back door of the inn.

00:43:12.386 --> 00:43:16.458
The bicycle was still by the wall.

00:43:16.518 --> 00:43:21.810
Holmes looked at the wheel and laughed quietly.

00:43:21.870 --> 00:43:25.530
A Dunlop tyre, Watson.

00:43:25.591 --> 00:43:34.197
Now, I must look through that upstairs window, so I need your back, Watson.

00:43:34.257 --> 00:43:41.282
Holmes stood on my back, but only for a second, and then he was down again.

00:43:41.342 --> 00:43:44.305
Come, my friend, he said.

00:43:44.365 --> 00:43:49.918
It's a long walk to the school, so let's start at once.

00:43:49.978 --> 00:43:55.718
I can give you all the answers to this mystery tomorrow."

00:43:55.778 --> 00:44:01.570
It was a long, cold, muddy walk back to the school.

00:44:01.630 --> 00:44:04.572
I went to bed at once.

00:44:04.632 --> 00:44:09.654
But homes went out again, to Mackelton, I think.

00:44:09.714 --> 00:44:17.764
I was very tired, and slept all night like a dead man.

00:44:17.824 --> 00:44:45.116
Chapter 6 Sherlock Holmes Talks to the Duke At eleven o'clock the next morning, Holmes and I were in the Duke's office at Holdeness Hall.

00:44:45.176 --> 00:44:49.360
Mr. Wilder came to speak to us.

00:44:49.420 --> 00:44:55.024
The duke can see no one today," he said to Holmes.

00:44:55.084 --> 00:44:58.346
Holmes looked at him coldly.

00:44:58.406 --> 00:45:02.148
The duke can see me, he said.

00:45:02.208 --> 00:45:05.980
Please tell him that I am here.

00:45:06.040 --> 00:45:12.073
After half an hour, the duke of holiness came into the room.

00:45:12.133 --> 00:45:18.368
He looked older, tired and ill.

00:45:18.428 --> 00:45:24.103
Holmes looked at James Wilder.

00:45:24.163 --> 00:45:30.804
I can speak more freely without your secretary here, sir.

00:45:30.864 --> 00:45:34.936
Very well, said the Duke tiredly.

00:45:34.996 --> 00:45:37.216
Please, James.

00:45:37.276 --> 00:45:46.540
James Wilder gave Holmes an angry look, but he went out of the room and shut the door.

00:45:46.600 --> 00:45:50.027
Holmes looked at the Duke.

00:45:50.087 --> 00:45:57.686
You are offering, I hear, £5,000 for news of your son.

00:45:57.746 --> 00:45:59.537
True.

00:45:59.597 --> 00:46:05.199
And another £1,000 for the name of the kidnapper.

00:46:05.259 --> 00:46:07.159
True.

00:46:07.220 --> 00:46:09.991
My friend smiled.

00:46:10.051 --> 00:46:14.522
I see your checkbook on the table, sir.

00:46:14.582 --> 00:46:19.398
I would like to have your check for £6,000.

00:46:19.458 --> 00:46:25.124
Mr. Sherlock Holmes, the Duke said angrily.

00:46:25.184 --> 00:46:27.735
What is this about?

00:46:27.795 --> 00:46:32.246
Do you have news of my son or not?

00:46:32.306 --> 00:46:35.837
Oh yes, said Holmes.

00:46:35.897 --> 00:46:40.068
The Duke's eyes never left Holmes's face.

00:46:40.129 --> 00:46:43.340
Where is my son?

00:46:43.400 --> 00:46:45.440
He said quietly.

00:46:45.500 --> 00:46:55.918
He is, or was last night, at the Green Man Inn, three kilometres along the road to Chesterfield.

00:46:55.978 --> 00:46:59.670
The Duke fell back in his chair.

00:46:59.730 --> 00:47:03.422
And the name of the kidnapper?

00:47:03.482 --> 00:47:08.645
Shillop Holmes' answer was a very surprising one.

00:47:08.705 --> 00:47:11.226
You, he said.

00:47:11.286 --> 00:47:15.008
And now, sir, your check, please.

00:47:15.069 --> 00:47:17.356
The Duke stood up.

00:47:17.417 --> 00:47:20.304
his face white and angry.

00:47:20.364 --> 00:47:26.288
Then he sat down again and put his face in his hands.

00:47:26.348 --> 00:47:30.730
It was some minutes before he spoke.

00:47:30.790 --> 00:47:33.492
How much do you know?

00:47:33.553 --> 00:47:35.214
He asked.

00:47:35.274 --> 00:47:40.226
I saw you with him last night, said Holmes.

00:47:40.286 --> 00:47:43.920
And how many people know about this?

00:47:43.980 --> 00:47:49.183
Only I and my friend here, Dr. Watson.

00:47:49.243 --> 00:47:56.614
The Duke took out a pen, opened his checkbook, and began to write.

00:47:56.674 --> 00:48:01.145
When I made this offer, I didn't know.

00:48:01.205 --> 00:48:04.956
He stopped, then began again.

00:48:05.016 --> 00:48:11.516
Are you and your friend going to talk about this, Mr. Holmes?

00:48:11.576 --> 00:48:14.685
I don't understand you, sir.

00:48:14.745 --> 00:48:16.354
said Holmes.

00:48:16.414 --> 00:48:24.178
I mean, nobody needs to know about this, this little family mystery.

00:48:24.238 --> 00:48:27.972
Just you and your friend Watson.

00:48:28.032 --> 00:48:34.916
Look, here is my check for 12,000 pounds.

00:48:34.976 --> 00:48:39.788
Holmes gave him a cold little smile.

00:48:39.848 --> 00:48:42.121
I'm sorry, sir.

00:48:42.181 --> 00:48:46.784
There is a dead man in this case, you remember?

00:48:46.844 --> 00:48:49.624
But that wasn't James!"

00:48:49.685 --> 00:48:51.315
cried the Duke.

00:48:51.375 --> 00:48:54.156
He knew nothing about it.

00:48:54.216 --> 00:49:01.649
He was very, very unhappy when he heard about the killing.

00:49:01.709 --> 00:49:04.860
Murder, said Holmes.

00:49:04.920 --> 00:49:08.071
But James wasn't there!

00:49:08.131 --> 00:49:15.647
And when he heard about it, He came to me at once and told me everything.

00:49:15.707 --> 00:49:19.448
Oh, Mr. Holmes, you must help him.

00:49:19.508 --> 00:49:21.059
You must.

00:49:21.119 --> 00:49:23.820
He is not the murderer.

00:49:23.880 --> 00:49:27.902
The murderer ran away last night.

00:49:27.962 --> 00:49:31.583
Holmes smiled again.

00:49:31.644 --> 00:49:35.908
I have a little more news for you, sir.

00:49:35.968 --> 00:49:42.842
The police met Mr. Ruben Hayes last night at Chesterfield Station.

00:49:42.902 --> 00:49:49.284
Mr. Hayes is not running anywhere for a very long time.

00:49:49.344 --> 00:49:55.355
The Duke looked at homes with an open mouth.

00:49:55.415 --> 00:49:59.196
You know everything, he said.

00:49:59.256 --> 00:50:02.866
But I am pleased to hear about Hayes.

00:50:02.926 --> 00:50:05.801
He was always a bad man.

00:50:05.861 --> 00:50:10.226
And that news can only help James.

00:50:10.286 --> 00:50:14.998
James, your secretary, said Holmes.

00:50:15.058 --> 00:50:16.639
No, sir.

00:50:16.699 --> 00:50:18.339
My son.

00:50:18.400 --> 00:50:23.822
James Wilder is my son.

00:50:23.882 --> 00:50:44.356
Chapter 7 The Duke's Son When the Duke said this, I was very surprised.

00:50:44.416 --> 00:50:47.808
But Holmes was surprised too.

00:50:47.868 --> 00:50:51.699
This is news to me, he said.

00:50:51.760 --> 00:50:54.261
Can you tell me more?

00:50:54.321 --> 00:51:00.024
The Duke stood up and walked round the room for a minute.

00:51:00.084 --> 00:51:04.276
I must tell you everything, he said.

00:51:04.336 --> 00:51:08.299
I didn't want to talk about it, but I must.

00:51:08.359 --> 00:51:10.959
I see that now.

00:51:11.019 --> 00:51:16.410
He sat down again and began his story.

00:51:16.471 --> 00:51:25.556
When I was a young man, Mr. Holmes, I was in love, no so much in love.

00:51:25.616 --> 00:51:33.340
It only happens to you once, and this woman was the love of my life.

00:51:33.400 --> 00:51:39.518
I wanted her to be my wife, but she died.

00:51:39.578 --> 00:51:46.808
She left me this one child and I loved him because of her.

00:51:46.868 --> 00:51:56.554
When I look in his face, I see her and remember her and can't stop loving her.

00:51:56.614 --> 00:52:01.206
I must have the boy near me because of this.

00:52:01.266 --> 00:52:08.949
But a government minister cannot tell the world about a love child like this.

00:52:09.009 --> 00:52:17.532
So, to the world, James is my young secretary, not my son.

00:52:17.592 --> 00:52:21.174
He knows that I am his father.

00:52:21.234 --> 00:52:26.326
He hates the Duchess because she is not his mother.

00:52:26.386 --> 00:52:33.300
And he hates my younger son, Arthur, because Arthur has everything.

00:52:33.360 --> 00:52:41.770
Arthur has a name, a famous father, houses, money, everything.

00:52:41.830 --> 00:52:45.142
James has nothing.

00:52:45.202 --> 00:52:57.758
Well, he has some money, of course, but he is just Mr. James Wilder, and he wants to be the Duke of Holderness one day.

00:52:57.818 --> 00:53:05.261
That's not possible, of course, but James can't understand that.

00:53:05.321 --> 00:53:10.738
And so, you see, I was afraid for Arthur.

00:53:10.798 --> 00:53:16.482
And that's why I sent him to Dr. Huxtable's school.

00:53:16.542 --> 00:53:20.486
And what does James do next?

00:53:20.546 --> 00:53:23.678
He kidnaps my poor Arthur.

00:53:23.738 --> 00:53:28.752
It changes nothing, but James can't see that.

00:53:28.812 --> 00:53:36.128
He wants me to say, yes, James, now you can be my first son.

00:53:36.188 --> 00:53:38.849
You can have everything.

00:53:38.909 --> 00:53:42.622
Arthur can be the number two son.

00:53:42.682 --> 00:53:45.154
But I can't do that.

00:53:45.214 --> 00:53:47.586
Of course I can't.

00:53:47.646 --> 00:53:55.873
James knew this man haze, you see, because haze worked for me once.

00:53:55.933 --> 00:54:02.539
James asked for haze's help, and the man was happy to do it.

00:54:02.599 --> 00:54:08.152
You remember my letter to Arthur on that last day?

00:54:08.212 --> 00:54:14.624
Well, James opened the letter and put in a note from him.

00:54:14.684 --> 00:54:21.768
That evening he cycled across the moor and met Arthur in ragged shore.

00:54:21.828 --> 00:54:25.900
He talked about the Duchess, Arthur's mother.

00:54:25.960 --> 00:54:29.641
She wants to see you, he told Arthur.

00:54:29.701 --> 00:54:32.272
She's waiting on the moor.

00:54:32.332 --> 00:54:38.394
Come back at midnight, and a man with a horse can take you to her.

00:54:38.454 --> 00:54:44.896
Of course, poor Arthur wanted to see his mother, so he came.

00:54:44.956 --> 00:54:51.518
Hayes was there with two horses, and they rode across them all.

00:54:51.578 --> 00:54:57.519
But the German teacher followed them, and Hayes killed him.

00:54:57.579 --> 00:55:02.172
Hayes then took Arthur to the Green Man.

00:55:02.232 --> 00:55:09.970
Well, Mr. Holmes, I knew nothing about any of this until the murder.

00:55:10.030 --> 00:55:15.272
James is a bad boy, but he does not murder people.

00:55:15.332 --> 00:55:20.796
When he heard the news, he came to me at once, crying.

00:55:20.856 --> 00:55:23.098
What could I do?

00:55:23.158 --> 00:55:26.990
I didn't want the world to know about this.

00:55:27.050 --> 00:55:30.952
So James went down to the green man.

00:55:31.013 --> 00:55:33.746
He told Hayes to run away.

00:55:33.806 --> 00:55:41.040
Because everybody knew about the murder now, and knew the murderer's name too.

00:55:41.100 --> 00:55:43.912
Hayes left at once.

00:55:43.973 --> 00:55:48.224
Later, I went down and saw Arthur.

00:55:48.284 --> 00:55:55.829
I left him there with Mrs. Hayes, because I couldn't say anything to the police just then.

00:55:55.889 --> 00:56:01.582
So, Mr. Holmes, now you know everything.

00:56:01.642 --> 00:56:03.215
Hmm.

00:56:03.275 --> 00:56:04.778
said Holmes.

00:56:04.838 --> 00:56:06.980
You help a murderer.

00:56:07.040 --> 00:56:09.502
You say nothing to the police.

00:56:09.562 --> 00:56:16.576
You leave your young son in a dirty inn, and you ask for my help."

00:56:16.636 --> 00:56:22.080
People never spoke to the Duke of Holderness like this, usually.

00:56:22.140 --> 00:56:26.364
His face was red, but he said nothing.

00:56:26.424 --> 00:56:31.768
First, said Holmes, we must bring Arthur home.

00:56:31.828 --> 00:56:33.378
Yes.

00:56:33.438 --> 00:56:36.108
The Duke said quietly.

00:56:36.168 --> 00:56:41.412
Holmes quickly wrote a note and took it out of the room.

00:56:41.472 --> 00:56:44.994
A minute later, he was back.

00:56:45.054 --> 00:56:50.728
Now, what are you going to do about Mr. James Wilder?

00:56:50.788 --> 00:56:52.270
He said.

00:56:52.330 --> 00:56:56.672
I understand you, Mr. Holmes, said the Duke.

00:56:56.732 --> 00:57:01.856
James is leaving me and going to Australia next week.

00:57:01.917 --> 00:57:03.247
Good.

00:57:03.307 --> 00:57:04.708
said Holmes.

00:57:04.768 --> 00:57:06.638
And the Duchess?

00:57:06.698 --> 00:57:15.994
Perhaps without James in the house, you and she, yes, I wrote to the Duchess this morning.

00:57:16.054 --> 00:57:18.536
Holmes stood up.

00:57:18.596 --> 00:57:24.128
Well, he said, Watson and I can go home now, I think.

00:57:24.188 --> 00:57:28.462
There is just one other small thing.

00:57:28.522 --> 00:57:39.251
This man haze took two horses across the moor, But the horse's feet made the tracks of a cow in the mud.

00:57:39.311 --> 00:57:42.322
How was this possible?

00:57:42.382 --> 00:57:47.394
The duke looked surprised and thought for a minute.

00:57:47.454 --> 00:57:55.967
Then he went away and came back two minutes later, with a glass box in his hands.

00:57:56.027 --> 00:57:59.723
In the box were some horseshoes.

00:57:59.783 --> 00:58:04.850
We found these shoes under the ground in the garden."

00:58:04.910 --> 00:58:06.522
The duke said.

00:58:06.582 --> 00:58:10.874
They are about five hundred years old, we think.

00:58:10.935 --> 00:58:16.777
The Holdeness family has a long and interesting past.

00:58:16.838 --> 00:58:22.050
Holmes opened the box and took out one shoe.

00:58:22.110 --> 00:58:29.729
It was a shoe for a horse's foot, but it looked like a cloven cow's foot.

00:58:29.789 --> 00:58:35.746
Holmes wet his finger, and ran it round the bottom of the shoe.

00:58:35.806 --> 00:58:39.738
A little mud came off on his finger.

00:58:39.798 --> 00:58:43.080
Thank you, said Holmes.

00:58:43.140 --> 00:58:46.672
He put the horse shoe back in its box.

00:58:46.732 --> 00:58:53.596
That shoe is the second most interesting thing in the north of England, he said.

00:58:53.656 --> 00:58:57.144
And the first asked the duke.

00:58:57.205 --> 00:59:06.264
Holmes took the check for £12,000 from the table and slowly put it into his notebook.

00:59:06.324 --> 00:59:09.906
I am a poor man, he said.

00:59:09.966 --> 00:59:16.398
He looked lovingly at the notebook, then put it carefully in his pocket.

